[[:db/retract 17592186118736 :answer-field/choices 17592186118737] [:db/retract 17592186118736 :answer-field/choices 17592186118738] [:db/retract 17592186118736 :answer-field/choices 17592186118739] [:db/retract 17592186118736 :answer-field/choices 17592186118740] [:db/retract 17592186118736 :answer-field/choices 17592186118741] {:db/id 17592186119658 :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y=2 \\\\ 2x+y=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nAccording to Cramer's rule, the unknown $x$ can be written as\n![](images/f5/f5c9b1c83ed648b56b47bd370ba5b15359521492087eda769d4122be99384a0f.svg)\nExpress $D_x$ in terms of a $2 \\times 2$ determinant." :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y=2 \\\\ 2x+y=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct $D_x$, we replace the first column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119788 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-659100c2-e69a-5015-bd46-ea6499418f4e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119599 :question/problem "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+2y=-1 \\\\ -3x+3y=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpress $y$ in terms of $2 \\times 2$ determinants." :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+2y=-1 \\\\ -3x+3y=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct $D_y$, we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 9\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 9\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119790 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1485a2c5-d3d5-5ae7-bfda-a8f34f74aef0" "question-9a324339-2131-569e-b62b-73969b420199"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119601 :question/problem "Let $\\langle x,3 \\rangle$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5x-2y=4 \\\\ x+ky=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\nI. ![](images/7d/7d767f03d04f1c35a774ef089d706894b2fe426995f1c7c050f8c5af0ef9e1e2.svg)\n\nII. ![](images/5a/5a9fe2dde8c8202f4532f745f0fac58ec649bdf39e928560ccaa2485d0f6f09e.svg)\n\nIII. ![](images/7e/7e2a9ca703f25107de026c84a8e7feb6099b48c7794ffdc166108358701feb8f.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120447 :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-6x+8y=-46 \\\\ 6x+5y=20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the unknown $y$ can be written as \n$y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{|\\begin{aligned}-6 & 8 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{aligned}|},$ \nwhere ${D}_{y}=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-6x+8y=-46 \\\\ 6x+5y=20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}-6 & \\,8 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$, we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}-6 & -46 \\\\ 6 & 20\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186329672 :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+12y=10 \\\\ 6x-7y=-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nAccording to Cramer's rule, the unknown $y$ can be written as \n$y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{|\\begin{aligned}5 & 12 \\\\ 6 & -7\\end{aligned}|}$, where ${D}_{y}=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+12y=10 \\\\ 6x-7y=-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 12 \\\\ 6 & -7\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$, we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 10 \\\\ 6 & -14\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186271976 :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x+11y=-23 \\\\ 5x-y=21.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the unknown $y$ can be written as \n$y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 11 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}|},$ \nwhere ${D}_{y}=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x+11y=-23 \\\\ 5x-y=21.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & \\,11 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$, we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -23 \\\\ 5 & 21\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186329671 :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x-3y=4 \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,2x-4y=-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nAccording to Cramer's rule, the unknown $x$ can be written as \n$x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}|}$, where ${D}_{x}=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x-3y=4 \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,2x-4y=-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe determinant of the coefficient  matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{x}$, we replace the first column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -12 & -4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186338763 :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+2y=7 \\\\ 3x-4y=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nAccording to Cramer's rule, the unknown $x$ can be written as \n$x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|}$, where ${D}_{x}=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+2y=7 \\\\ 3x-4y=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{x}$, we replace the first column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-659100c2-e69a-5015-bd46-ea6499418f4e" :question/id #uuid "659100c2-e69a-5015-bd46-ea6499418f4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-77396" :question/problem "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y=2 \\\\ 2x+3y=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $x=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y=2 \\\\ 2x+3y=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we construct ${D}_{x}$, we replace the first column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4d79a455-f937-543f-8ebe-441cfa187191"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4d79a455-f937-543f-8ebe-441cfa187191" :answer-field/id #uuid "4d79a455-f937-543f-8ebe-441cfa187191" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1c2929bd-edc2-5508-beb1-1d9807142bf1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d56c8d4b-ec4f-5319-9ebf-a207cab9ae06" "answer-c159eb9f-4f2c-5439-9834-15476295ce88" "answer-f7c1f9ea-b9de-5947-a51a-a2f5c3cb34c7" "answer-1c2929bd-edc2-5508-beb1-1d9807142bf1" "answer-f0696591-4c24-54b6-8b14-e466d380abaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d56c8d4b-ec4f-5319-9ebf-a207cab9ae06" :answer/id #uuid "d56c8d4b-ec4f-5319-9ebf-a207cab9ae06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c159eb9f-4f2c-5439-9834-15476295ce88" :answer/id #uuid "c159eb9f-4f2c-5439-9834-15476295ce88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7c1f9ea-b9de-5947-a51a-a2f5c3cb34c7" :answer/id #uuid "f7c1f9ea-b9de-5947-a51a-a2f5c3cb34c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c2929bd-edc2-5508-beb1-1d9807142bf1" :answer/id #uuid "1c2929bd-edc2-5508-beb1-1d9807142bf1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f0696591-4c24-54b6-8b14-e466d380abaa" :answer/id #uuid "f0696591-4c24-54b6-8b14-e466d380abaa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186393681 :question/problem "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4x+2y=5 \\\\ x-3y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $y=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4x+2y=5 \\\\ x-3y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$ we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120437 :question/problem "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y=2 \\\\ x+5y=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $x=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y=2 \\\\ x+5y=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we construct ${D}_{x}$, we replace the first column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 10 & 5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 10 & 5\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186118736 :answer-field/correct "answer-d2f9ea97-6403-5269-8dae-1465c6fa454a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e54fae11-f4e6-587e-bf65-bc9a931e3cc7" "answer-fefcd620-c9c3-502f-a8a1-81af7c238754" "answer-d2f9ea97-6403-5269-8dae-1465c6fa454a" "answer-8fa3964d-0f84-58b2-a2df-245a34859a58" "answer-6feb8d82-ec98-5ab3-916e-e0964f921e81"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e54fae11-f4e6-587e-bf65-bc9a931e3cc7" :answer/id #uuid "e54fae11-f4e6-587e-bf65-bc9a931e3cc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\,\\,-3 \\\\ 1 & \\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 10 & \\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}|}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fefcd620-c9c3-502f-a8a1-81af7c238754" :answer/id #uuid "fefcd620-c9c3-502f-a8a1-81af7c238754" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,2 & \\,\\,-3 \\\\ 10 & \\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -5\\end{aligned}|}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2f9ea97-6403-5269-8dae-1465c6fa454a" :answer/id #uuid "d2f9ea97-6403-5269-8dae-1465c6fa454a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,2 & \\,\\,-3 \\\\ 10 & \\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}|}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8fa3964d-0f84-58b2-a2df-245a34859a58" :answer/id #uuid "8fa3964d-0f84-58b2-a2df-245a34859a58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,2 & \\,\\,-3 \\\\ 15 & \\,\\,\\,1\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}|}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6feb8d82-ec98-5ab3-916e-e0964f921e81" :answer/id #uuid "6feb8d82-ec98-5ab3-916e-e0964f921e81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,3 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ 10 & \\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}|}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186329669 :question/problem "Consider the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4x+6y=32 \\\\ 3x+5y=26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $x=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4x+6y=32 \\\\ 3x+5y=26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we construct ${D}_{x}$, we replace the first column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}32 & 6 \\\\ 26 & 5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}32 & 6 \\\\ 26 & 5\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186388632 :question/problem "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+8y=-14 \\\\ 5x+4y=13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $y=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+8y=-14 \\\\ 5x+4y=13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$ we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -14 \\\\ 5 & 13\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & -14 \\\\ 5 & 13\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186329702 :question/problem "Let $⟨-1,y⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+5y=k \\\\ 2x-y=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\nI. $|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|=-13$\n\nII. $|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|=-1$\n\nIII. $|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|=13$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186271990 :question/problem "Let $⟨x,3⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}kx+3y=1 \\\\ 7x-2y=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\nI. $-3|\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|$\n\nII. $3|\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|$\n\nIII. $|\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}|=3|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120448 :question/problem "Let $⟨x,3⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y=10 \\\\ kx-4y=12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\nI. $3|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ k & -4\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ k & 12\\end{aligned}|$\n\nII. $|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ k & -4\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ k & 12\\end{aligned}|$\n\nIII. $|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ k & -4\\end{aligned}|=3|\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ k & 12\\end{aligned}|$" :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ k & -4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ k & 12\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ k & 12\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ k & -4\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ 3|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ k & -4\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ k & 12\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186118802 :answer-field/correct 17592186118805 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-1485a2c5-d3d5-5ae7-bfda-a8f34f74aef0" :question/id #uuid "1485a2c5-d3d5-5ae7-bfda-a8f34f74aef0" :question/math-academy-id "q-77402" :question/problem "Let $⟨2,y⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4x+ky=5 \\\\ x+2y=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\nI. $|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|$\n\nII. $2|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|$\n\nIII. $|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=2|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|$" :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ 2|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1aec48af-7f8c-53fd-bb3d-101ace543e43"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1aec48af-7f8c-53fd-bb3d-101ace543e43" :answer-field/id #uuid "1aec48af-7f8c-53fd-bb3d-101ace543e43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-37e0bd1c-a3ae-5f52-a82d-3a71181d02f2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-13abba68-c603-520c-b95e-bae74246f467" "answer-ed90928a-c1d1-55de-ac12-d5f61d39fd02" "answer-8d3a2a97-810a-5f83-ae72-fc21a76e36d4" "answer-37e0bd1c-a3ae-5f52-a82d-3a71181d02f2" "answer-45f349a4-8a10-5b19-b4f8-85a49af13560"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13abba68-c603-520c-b95e-bae74246f467" :answer/id #uuid "13abba68-c603-520c-b95e-bae74246f467" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ed90928a-c1d1-55de-ac12-d5f61d39fd02" :answer/id #uuid "ed90928a-c1d1-55de-ac12-d5f61d39fd02" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d3a2a97-810a-5f83-ae72-fc21a76e36d4" :answer/id #uuid "8d3a2a97-810a-5f83-ae72-fc21a76e36d4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-37e0bd1c-a3ae-5f52-a82d-3a71181d02f2" :answer/id #uuid "37e0bd1c-a3ae-5f52-a82d-3a71181d02f2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45f349a4-8a10-5b19-b4f8-85a49af13560" :answer/id #uuid "45f349a4-8a10-5b19-b4f8-85a49af13560" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9a324339-2131-569e-b62b-73969b420199" :question/id #uuid "9a324339-2131-569e-b62b-73969b420199" :question/math-academy-id "q-42985" :question/problem "Let $⟨-12,y⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}7x+9y=42 \\\\ kx+10y=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\nI. $|\\begin{aligned}7 & 9 \\\\ k & 10\\end{aligned}|=-12$\n\nII. $|\\begin{aligned}7 & 9 \\\\ k & 10\\end{aligned}|=-38$\n\nIII. $|\\begin{aligned}7 & 9 \\\\ k & 10\\end{aligned}|=456$" :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}7 & 9 \\\\ k & 10\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}42 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 10\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =420+36 \\\\  & =456.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D} \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{456}{|\\begin{aligned}7 & 9 \\\\ k & 10\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}7 & 9 \\\\ k & 10\\end{aligned}| & =\\frac{456}{-12} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}7 & 9 \\\\ k & 10\\end{aligned}| & =-38\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cb7f776c-eb99-528b-aabd-b4033c71b940"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cb7f776c-eb99-528b-aabd-b4033c71b940" :answer-field/id #uuid "cb7f776c-eb99-528b-aabd-b4033c71b940" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bd29ef89-365b-598b-abba-79648038c1f5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3cc8305b-aa26-5938-bd09-82bace4ba090" "answer-1f13ed83-8c4f-597b-9f02-b31307021e5b" "answer-f4490cc5-d61d-513b-835c-43fda69e74cc" "answer-bd29ef89-365b-598b-abba-79648038c1f5" "answer-742473cb-daf1-51d3-8173-d6d820c2cd4a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3cc8305b-aa26-5938-bd09-82bace4ba090" :answer/id #uuid "3cc8305b-aa26-5938-bd09-82bace4ba090" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f13ed83-8c4f-597b-9f02-b31307021e5b" :answer/id #uuid "1f13ed83-8c4f-597b-9f02-b31307021e5b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4490cc5-d61d-513b-835c-43fda69e74cc" :answer/id #uuid "f4490cc5-d61d-513b-835c-43fda69e74cc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd29ef89-365b-598b-abba-79648038c1f5" :answer/id #uuid "bd29ef89-365b-598b-abba-79648038c1f5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-742473cb-daf1-51d3-8173-d6d820c2cd4a" :answer/id #uuid "742473cb-daf1-51d3-8173-d6d820c2cd4a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121027 :tutorial/content "**Cramer's Rule** is a method for solving a linear system of equations using determinants.\n\nSuppose we have a square system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ![](images/c7/c7ef883a1d4dd8c1fc0fc8fbde5ed80c9a5229650fc77c77559b71552370c35b.svg) Then Cramer's rule states that\n\n$$\nx =  \\dfrac{D_x}{D}, \\qquad y = \\dfrac{D_y}{D}\n$$\n\nis the unique solution of the system, where\n![](images/b1/b13ecd10395fe0977d04d627179667cbca207fcf4015a89d43df0e69765f1f5e.svg)\n\nFor example, let's use Cramer's rule to solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-2y=-1 \\\\ -1x+2y=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe start by finding the **determinant of the coefficient matrix**:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $D_x$ and $D_y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 2-3\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =4 \\\\ {D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot 3-(-1)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to the system is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D}=\\frac{4}{4}=1, \\\\ y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{8}{4}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIt is common to write the solutions to a linear system as a vector. So, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\left< x,y \\right> = \\left< 1,2 \\right>.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119997 :activity/title "Cramer's Rule for 2x2 Systems of Linear Equations" :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
